  "description": "Two storey detached outbuilding to rear for use as Tyre fitting shop/Valeting shop/Storage (Demolition of detached outbuilding)",
  "development_type": "Minor retail and service",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify; text-indent: -18pt;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; The proposed\r\ndevelopment could result in unacceptable impacts upon the amenities of\r\nresidential properties in terms of noise and general disturbance. No supporting\r\ntechnical information relating to noise has been submitted by the applicant to\r\notherwise demonstrate that adequate measures would be in place to prevent\r\nadverse impacts to neighbouring residential amenity. The development therefore\r\nfails to comply with Policies D13 and D14 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy\r\nGR1(C) of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify; text-indent: -18pt;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;By virtue of the proposed building’s design\r\nresulting in the loss of two on-site parking spaces and the intensification of\r\nthe existing use, it is considered that the proposed development would give\r\nrise to an increase in coming and goings by way of vehicular movements and\r\nresult in additional pressure on off-street parking to serve the commercial\r\noperations. The development is found to be contrary to Paragraph 117 of the\r\nNPPF (2024) and policy M2 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
